				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4874276&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606894928" alt="TheAlienBaby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4874276)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;" >TheAlienBaby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606893805 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Dec 2020 07:23</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13868107/scp-idea-leviathan-of-the-midnight-sun-mitternachtsonne">SCP idea- Leviathan of The midnight Sun (Mitternachtsonne)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4834144">
									

<p>Hey there Anonymousauthor, I’ll be critting your idea today!<br />
Note that I am not an official reviewer, so take what I say with a grain of salt. With that being said, let’s begin the crit!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Section-by-Section</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Wooooosh</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Elevator Pitch</span></p>
<p>So your SCP is some kind of large aquatic creature (nice physical description btw). However, I have much the same concerns as Captain Cold in regards to how the Foundation knows it’s appearance so well. Not only this, but why are they such problems associated with looking at it? Is it cognitohazardous? Also:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[&#8230;]located somewhere in the Atlantic at a Site known as The Ring.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would have assumed you meant in or around the <a href="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ring_of_Fire">Ring of Fire</a>, but that’s in the Pacific. So where is this Ring? And why was it constructed?</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Central Narrative</span></p>
<p>You explain the abilities of this Leviathan in more detail here, where it mutates the surrounding sea life and makes them hostile. Unfortunately, this feels&#8230; very similar to <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3069">SCP-3069</a>, in that the anomaly mutates all surrounding sea life. Not only this, but like Angryman22 and Captain Cold I am concerned about this narrative, which seems to consist only of research missions ending in death. I’d recommend changing it.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Hook/Attention Grabber</span></p>
<p>Ok, but why can it alter the salinity around itself? This just seems like an extra ability tacked onto the anomaly in order to increase the pressure it puts on the Foundation.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;don’t&nbsp;know&nbsp;about&nbsp;this</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The idea is similar in ability to SCP-3069, the narrative is cliche and uninteresting, and the hook adds an extra ability randomly, making the whole thing feel a bit disjointed.</p>
<p>As an extra explanation for the narrative, explorations that end in death are completely fine (I actually have a soft spot for them myself). However, people usually expect some kind of twist, deeper narrative, or reveal in these exploration logs, so work on that.</p>
<p>I’d recommend three things:<br />
1. Find something to seperate this concept from SCP-3069.<br />
2. Work on your narrative! Brainstorm ideas, think of an emotion you want your readers to feel, and let that guide the direction your story takes.<br />
3. Check out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/comprehensive-guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for some great essays on ideation and story-ing!</p>
<p>And finally, to sum up your concept in one sentence<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-844142-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-844142-1')">1</a></sup>:<br />
A large leviathan-like creature (presumably cognitohazardous) that mutates all the surrounding sea life and increases the salinity of the water surrounding it, with devastating effects on its environment.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyway, that’s it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps!</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-844142-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-844142-1')">1</a>. This is to help you get an idea of the bare bones of what a critter sees when they read your summary. You may find something you don’t like here, or that we’re getting the wrong impression.</div>
</div>

